{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLfU7zWRwDQ2WxcbAyfP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The missing-tests scanner is now a starter role, with the scan script, a pinned Dockerfile, a config entry, test updates and docs. `GOPROXY=off go test ./internal/roles ./internal/initcmd` passes, and `go vet -tags integration ./internal/roles` is clean. I wrote the Docker integration test and compiled it but did not run it, because there is no Docker or network here. The report is at `.ard/213/worker-engineer.md`.\n\n- **Scan behaviour:** it runs each Go module's own tests with coverage. If a module fails to build or its tests fail, it exits 1 with no output, so autoclose never acts on partial data. Missing `go` exits 2.\n- **Opt-outs:** it honours human-owned `ignore` and `no-coverage` files next to `scan`.\n- **Config:** the starter entry is `every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 10, autoclose: true`.\n- **Docs:** I edited `docs/proposal.md` and `docs/layout.md`. I did not touch `CLAUDE.md`, because the layout list now lives in `docs/layout.md`.\n\n- **Network need:** the scan does not set `GOPROXY=off`, so repositories with dependencies need egress to the module proxy.\n- **Slow tests:** the `internal/roles` tests now take about 110 s, because each fixture runs `go test`.\n- **Go version in tests:** the scan tests substitute the real Go version for `go1.test` in each fixture's expected output."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":972,"cache_read_input_tokens":39993,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":972},"output_tokens":503,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c566320b-09c8-4476-8bc3-25d5a8790bc1","uuid":"f2fb0c95-6632-